<?XML version="1.0"?>
<CHANNEL HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/default.htm">
  <TITLE>Active Channel Tutorial</TITLE>
  <ABSTRACT>An Active Channel with dynamic styles, content, animations, and more.</ABSTRACT>
  <LOGO HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/actlogo2.gif" STYLE="IMAGE-WIDE" />
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/default.htm">
    <TITLE>Introduction</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn how to create your own Active Channel Content with CDF files and Dynamic HTML.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr1.htm">
    <TITLE>1 Creating Active Channel Content</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>The four steps to creating active channel content: a CDF file, Dynamic HTML, updates, and getting your channel listed in the Channel Guide.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr2.htm">
    <TITLE>2 Interacting with a CDF File</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Shows you how channels are added to the channel pane, and how subscriptions and scheduling work.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr3.htm">
    <TITLE>3 Inside the CDF File</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn about the structure of the CDF file, the CDF tags, and how to add screen savers and desktop components to your channel.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr4.htm">
    <TITLE>4 Dynamic HTML Overview</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>An overview of the important features of Dynamic HTML, including client-side advantages, working examples of Dynamic HTML, sample web pages, and an overview of the Object Model.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr5.htm">
    <TITLE>5 Dynamic Styles</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn how to use dynamic styles with cascading style sheets to create responsive, interactive web pages. You'll also learn how to apply visual filters and transitions, and control visibility and display of page elements.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr6.htm">
    <TITLE>6 Dynamic Positioning</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn how to position elements on a web page (absolute and relative), how to create animations, and how to use Z-ORDER to control layering of page elements.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr7.htm">
    <TITLE>7 Dynamic Content</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Dynamic HTML allows you to change anything on the page at any time, on the fly, without reloading from the server. You can even change the underlying HTML on the page to create stunning interactivity.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr8.htm">
    <TITLE>8 Data Binding</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn how to write client-side scripts that can access server-side data, and manipulate it on the client. This allows you to build powerful, data-intensive applications using scripts.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <ITEM HREF="http://www.microsoft.com/workshop/prog/ie4/channels/tutorial/fr9.htm">
    <TITLE>9 Multimedia Effects</TITLE>
    <ABSTRACT>Learn how to use mutlimedia effects such as: moving objects on a path, sequencing effects, sprites, and structured graphics.</ABSTRACT>
  </ITEM>
  <SCHEDULE ENDDATE="1997-11-30">
    <INTERVALTIME DAY="1"/>
    <EARLIESTTIME HOUR="12"/>
    <LATESTTIME HOUR="18"/>
  </SCHEDULE>
</CHANNEL>
